1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,742
In this lesson, you'll ask customers
for reviews by text and email,

2
00:00:04,742 --> 00:00:09,743
one at a time or completely automatically,
and track who has actually left one.

3
00:00:09,743 --> 00:00:13,668
More reviews mean more trust,
and better visibility on Google.

4
00:00:14,528 --> 00:00:18,369
The businesses with the
most reviews aren't luckier.

5
00:00:18,369 --> 00:00:21,989
They simply ask every
happy customer, every time.

6
00:00:21,989 --> 00:00:25,904
Here, more than 300 requests
turned into 127 reviews.

7
00:00:26,757 --> 00:00:28,616
Let's send one by hand first.

8
00:00:28,616 --> 00:00:32,142
Click Send Review Request,
then search for the contact.

9
00:00:32,142 --> 00:00:36,757
Mia Harris has just finished her
whitening session, so let's select her.

10
00:00:36,757 --> 00:00:40,219
The best time to ask is while
the experience is fresh.

11
00:00:41,069 --> 00:00:42,387
Choose SMS or email.

12
00:00:42,387 --> 00:00:47,924
Text messages usually get the most reviews,
because people read them within minutes.

13
00:00:47,924 --> 00:00:50,890
Email works well for
customers who prefer it,

14
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:53,461
or when you don't have a mobile number.

15
00:00:53,461 --> 00:00:56,625
The preview shows exactly
what Mia will receive,

16
00:00:56,625 --> 00:00:59,591
with her name and your
review link filled in.

17
00:01:00,441 --> 00:01:01,089
Click Send.

18
00:01:01,089 --> 00:01:05,390
The request is on its way, and it
appears at the top of the Requests tab.

19
00:01:06,242 --> 00:01:08,372
Here you can follow every request.

20
00:01:08,372 --> 00:01:10,064
Delivered means it arrived.

21
00:01:10,064 --> 00:01:12,757
Clicked means they
opened your review link.

22
00:01:12,757 --> 00:01:15,138
And Reviewed means they left a review.

23
00:01:15,138 --> 00:01:18,709
Together, these tell you how
well your asking is working.

24
00:01:18,709 --> 00:01:22,593
If lots of people click but few
review, try a shorter message,

25
00:01:22,593 --> 00:01:24,285
or a different time of day.

26
00:01:25,135 --> 00:01:29,970
Sending by hand works, but
the real win is automation.

27
00:01:29,970 --> 00:01:36,955
Most of these requests came from a
workflow called Review Request After Visit.

28
00:01:36,955 --> 00:01:43,849
It sends a request automatically whenever
an appointment is marked as showed.

29
00:01:43,849 --> 00:01:47,879
You'll build workflows
like this in module 9.

30
00:01:48,729 --> 00:01:51,310
Now let's fine-tune when requests go out.

31
00:01:51,310 --> 00:01:54,458
Open the Settings tab, and
choose Review requests.

32
00:01:55,316 --> 00:01:56,843
For SMS, choose Custom.

33
00:01:56,843 --> 00:02:02,020
Send the request 2 hours after the visit,
while the experience is still fresh.

34
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:06,932
If they don't click, Kyntlo reminds
them every 3 days, up to 2 more times,

35
00:02:06,932 --> 00:02:09,056
and stops as soon as they click.

36
00:02:09,912 --> 00:02:11,738
You can edit the message too.

37
00:02:11,738 --> 00:02:17,028
Keep it short, warm and personal, and always
keep the review link placeholder in it.

38
00:02:17,028 --> 00:02:20,617
Use the customer's first name,
and mention your business,

39
00:02:20,617 --> 00:02:22,381
so it never feels like spam.

40
00:02:22,381 --> 00:02:23,388
Then click Save.

41
00:02:24,239 --> 00:02:25,303
Here's a pro tip.

42
00:02:25,303 --> 00:02:28,870
Time your requests for the
moment customers are happiest.

43
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:32,249
For a dentist, that's right
after a whitening session,

44
00:02:32,249 --> 00:02:34,189
or the day the braces come off.

45
00:02:34,189 --> 00:02:37,882
For you, it might be delivery
day, or the end of a project.

46
00:02:37,882 --> 00:02:40,948
Set your workflow's trigger
to match that moment.

47
00:02:41,799 --> 00:02:44,164
Now the reviews will start rolling in.

48
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:48,396
In the next lesson, you'll reply
to them in seconds with Reviews AI.

49
00:02:48,396 --> 00:02:49,267
See you there.
